BOCL Common Lisp
****************

‘bocl’ is a Common Lisp implementation built from a small C kernel plus
a runtime-loaded Lisp prelude.

* Menu:

* Overview::            What bocl is.
* Invocation::          Running bocl from the command line.
* Error handling::      The ‘--on-error’ option.
* Files::               Installed layout and start-up files.
* Debugger::            The minimal debugger.
* Further reading::     Manuals and specifications.


