2 Invocation
************

     bocl [options]

   The most common options are summarized below; see ‘bocl(1)’ for the
full list.

‘-h, --help’
     Print a usage summary and exit.
‘-V, --version’
     Print ‘(LISP-IMPLEMENTATION-VERSION)’ and exit.
‘-l, --load FILE’
     Load FILE.
‘-x, -e, --eval FORM’
     Evaluate FORM (quote it for the shell).
‘-p, --package PACKAGE’
     Start in PACKAGE.
‘-b, --batch’
     Exit on end of file on ‘*STANDARD-INPUT*’.
‘-n, --norc, --no-init’
     Do not load ‘~/.boclrc’.
‘--no-prelude’
     Bare kernel only -- do not load the prelude.
‘--on-error ACTION’
     What to do when an unhandled error reaches the top level: one of
     ‘exit’ (the default), ‘debug’, ‘abort’, ‘appease’.  *Note Error
     handling::.
‘-q, --quit’
     Quit when argument processing is done (otherwise enter the REPL).


