5 The minimal debugger
**********************

When an unhandled ‘SERIOUS-CONDITION’ reaches the top level under
‘--on-error debug’ (or via ‘INVOKE-DEBUGGER’ / ‘BREAK’), bocl enters a
minimal debugger: it prints the condition, a backtrace and the available
restarts, then runs a read-eval-print loop.  Keyword commands
(‘:backtrace’, ‘:restart’, ‘:continue’, ‘:abort’, ‘:quit’, ‘:help’) and
bare restart numbers select actions; any other form is evaluated as Lisp
in the error's dynamic context.  The complete specification is in
‘debugger-specifications.org’.


